---
title: Chicken Thai Green Curry
description: Tender chicken thighs simmered in a fragrant coconut green curry sauce with edamame, sugar snap peas, and garden beans — served over fluffy basmati rice.
source: personal
author: personal
changes:
  - Substitute boneless skinless chicken thighs for chicken breast
  - Use 2 lb chicken
  - Replace every 3/4 cup measure with 2 cups (basmati rice, frozen edamame, frozen garden beans)
  - Triple all other ingredients
servings: 6
time required: 40 minutes
course: main
cuisine: Thai
tags:
  - chicken
  - curry
  - coconut
  - thai
  - skillet
  - quick
  - scaling
---

Cook @basmati rice{2%cups} according to package directions. Keep warm.

Dice @boneless skinless chicken thighs{2%lb} into bite-sized chunks. Heat @vegetable oil{2%tbsp} in a #large skillet{} or wok over medium heat. Add the chicken, season with @kosher salt{} and @black pepper{}, and cook, stirring occasionally, until no pink remains and an instant-read thermometer reads 165°F, about ~{8-10%minutes}.

Add @onion{3}(brown, sliced) and cook until softened, about ~{3-4%minutes}. Stir in @Thai green curry paste{6%tbsp} and cook until fragrant, about ~{4-5%minutes}.

Add @coconut milk{1 1/2%cans}, @fish sauce{2%tbsp}, @frozen edamame beans{2%cups}, @sugar snap peas{2%cups}, and @frozen garden beans{2%cups}. Cook until the vegetables are tender and the sauce is fragrant, about ~{8-10%minutes}.

Garnish with @fresh cilantro{}(chopped), @scallions{}(sliced), and @fresh chili{}(sliced). Serve over the rice.
